          "court": "United States Court of Appeals for the Seventh Circuit",
          "year": 2002,
          "date_decided": "2002-08-30",
          "holding": "The court held that the credible-evidence standard combined with a belated post-deprivation hearing denied child-care workers adequate process when DCFS disclosed indicated findings to their employers, though the individual DCFS defendants were immune and the private employers were not state actors.",
          "relevance": "Judicial findings of systemic register-process failure supply an external performance check on the state agency.",
          "quote": "we conclude that the credible evidence standard, operating in conjunction with a belated post-deprivation hearing, failed to afford adequate process to Ms. Doyle and Mr. Konold",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/779307/elizabeth-doyle-v-camelot-care-centers-incorporated-a-delaware/",
